From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: cabinet: implement the Compression API (MSZIP)

cabinet.dll exported none of the Compression API (ordinals 30-35 and 40-45),
so `winget show` died in CreateDecompressor: winget's community source keeps
its manifests MSZIP-compressed with it.

Implement Create/Close/Reset/Set/QueryCompressor and ...Decompressor,
Compress and Decompress for COMPRESS_ALGORITHM_MSZIP and _NULL, in buffer
mode and with COMPRESS_RAW. Buffer mode frames the data with a 24-byte header
(signature 0a 51 e5 c0, header size, a checksum byte, the algorithm, the
uncompressed and chunk sizes) and length-prefixed chunks; an MSZIP chunk is a
series of "CK" blocks, raw deflate of at most 32 KiB each with the previous
32 KiB as dictionary. The checksum byte is the low byte of the CRC-32 of the
other 23 header bytes -- established against real buffers from winget's
source, and checked on decompression. XPRESS, XPRESS_HUFF and LZMS report
ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED for now. Adds include/compressapi.h.

Gate: test/compress-gate.sh.

